#: include/global_settings.php
msgid ""
"There are four methods for determining a User's Graph Permissions.  The "
"first is 'Permissive'.  Under the 'Permissive' setting, a User only needs "
"access to either the Graph, Device or Graph Template to gain access to the "
"Graphs that apply to them.  Under 'Restrictive', the User must have access "
"to the Graph, the Device, and the Graph Template to gain access to the "
"Graph.  These first two methods have scalability problems for very large "
"installs.  So, two additional options are available.  They are 'Device "
"Based', which means if you have access to the Device, you get access to it's"
" Graphs.  And lastly 'Graph Template Based', which means if you have access "
"to the 'Graph Template' you get access to all Device Graphs of that "
"Template."
msgstr ""
"Det finns fyra metoder för att avgöra en användares grafbehörighet. Med "
"”Tillåtande” räcker åtkomst till grafen, enheten eller grafmallen för att få"
" åtkomst till motsvarande grafer. Med ”Restriktiv” krävs åtkomst till alla "
"tre. Dessa två metoder kan ha skalbarhetsproblem i mycket stora "
"installationer. De två andra alternativen är ”Enhetsbaserad”, där åtkomst "
"till enheten ger åtkomst till dess grafer, och ”Grafmallbaserad”, där "
"åtkomst till grafmallen ger åtkomst till alla enhetsgrafer som använder "
"mallen."

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Permissive"
msgstr "Tillåtande"

#: include/global_settings.php
msgid "Device Based"
msgstr "Enhetsbaserad"

